// Cut ChatGPT/Codex usage. Every agent step re-sends the whole context, so the goal is fewer steps and fewer runs.
// - Minimal tool profile + only what the agent uses: shell (exec), messaging, silent cron replies, skill reads,
//   the web (browser, Codex-hosted web_search, web_fetch), and reminders from chat (automations).
// - NO `process` tool: exec then always waits for the command (no backgrounding, no polling, and no extra
//   "command finished" wake-up runs, which were ~40% of runs on 2026-11-06). 570 s cap stays under the
//   harness's 600 s tool budget; a cut-off `ia search` is simply re-run (finished privacy checks are cached).
// - Telegram DM history pasted into each run: 4 recent messages instead of 10.
// Apply (container running):  docker compose -f ~/dingding/docker/compose.yaml exec -T openclaw openclaw config patch --stdin < ops/openclaw-tools.patch.json5
// Roll back: echo '{tools:{profile:"full",alsoAllow:null,exec:{timeoutSeconds:null}},channels:{telegram:{dmHistoryLimit:null}}}' | (same command)
{
  tools: {
    profile: "minimal",
    alsoAllow: ["exec", "message", "heartbeat_respond", "skills_read", "browser", "web_search", "web_fetch",
                "automations"],   // reminders from chat; each firing = one short model run (rules in inbox skill)
    exec: { timeoutSeconds: 570 },
  },
  channels: { telegram: { dmHistoryLimit: 4 } },
}
